From 2b9ddff082cefc6b58c184ec4932b91b98019a6c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 11:51:27 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 05/13] Round 5: Serialize traces directly from typed rows

Store the trace as Option<Vec<[f64; 4]>> in the typed metrics and
serialize it directly instead of building a serde_json::Value tree of
arrays. Reserve the trace for the expected step count, capped at the
10,000-row trace limit. A unit test checks the limit (10,001 steps,
invalid, at dt 1e-4) and that a short trace has one row per step and
ends at the horizon.

Workload: trace (12 traced full records, 62 steps each, one worker).
Before median: 0.2343 ms. After median: 0.1047 ms. Speedup: 2.24x.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
